{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015hHgSnmQRQcK5y2sGYAfbk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: t3-002\n2\ttier: 3\n3\ttitle: X-band maritime search radar architecture under frame-time, power, and availability floors\n4\tsummary: >\n5\t  Design the architecture of an X-band (9.5 GHz) naval search phased array\n6\t  detecting a low-altitude Swerling-1 target over sea clutter. The design\n7\t  must achieve the required worst-case detection probability over an\n8\t  evaluation envelope withheld from this brief (target range and RCS, scan\n9\t  angle, sea state, and random element-failure draws), sweep its assigned\n10\t  search volume within the frame-time budget, and still meet its\n11\t  pattern spec at end of mission after component failures. Aperture size,\n12\t  per-element power, waveform (PRF, pulses per dwell), taper, and\n13\t  quantization pull against each other: a bigger aperture narrows the beam\n14\t  and multiplies beam positions until the frame budget breaks; fewer\n15\t  pulses lose integration gain and force per-element power up, heating the\n16\t  junction and eroding end-of-mission availability.\n17\t\n18\tcontext:\n19\t  mission: xband_maritime_search\n20\t  radar:\n21\t    frequency_ghz: 9.5\n22\t    bandwidth_mhz: 5.0\n23\t    pfa: 1.0e-6\n24\t    pd_required: 0.7\n25\t    noise_figure_db: 3.5\n26\t    antenna_height_m: 30.0\n27\t    cfar_type: CA\n28\t    cfar_ref_cells: 16\n29\t    cfar_guard_cells: 2\n30\t  search:\n31\t    az_extent_deg: 60.0\n32\t    el_extent_deg: 15.0\n33\t    frame_time_ms: 3000.0\n34\t    beam_overhead_us: 50.0\n35\t  nominal_scenario:\n36\t    range_km: 13.0\n37\t    rcs_dbsm: 6.0\n38\t    scan_deg: 25.0\n39\t    sea_state: 3\n40\t    target_height_m: 5.0\n41\t  evaluation_envelope_bounds:\n42\t    # Clutter-limited and noise-limited points have different reach:\n43\t    # points with sea clutter (sea_state > 0) occur only within\n44\t    # clutter_range_km_max and at rcs >= rcs_dbsm_min_clutter; clear-sea\n45\t    # points extend to range_km_max at rcs >= rcs_dbsm_min.\n46\t    range_km_max: 26.0\n47\t    rcs_dbsm_min: 2.0\n48\t    clutter_range_km_max: 14.0\n49\t    rcs_dbsm_min_clutter: 6.0\n50\t    scan_deg_max: 40.0\n51\t    sea_state_max: 3\n52\t    element_failure_rate: 0.02\n53\t  waveform_bounds:\n54\t    prf_hz_min: 500.0\n55\t    prf_hz_max: 3000.0\n56\t    n_pulses_min: 1\n57\t    n_pulses_max: 64\n58\t  constraints:\n59\t    prime_power_ceiling_w: 5500.0\n60\t    unit_cost_ceiling_usd: 650000.0\n61\t  reliability:\n62\t    component_mtbfs:\n63\t      lna: 500000.0\n64\t      phase_shifter: 2000000.0\n65\t      attenuator: 3000000.0\n66\t      switch: 1000000.0\n67\t      control_asic: 1000000.0\n68\t    thermal_resistance_c_per_w: 40.0\n69\t    ambient_temp_c: 40.0\n70\t    mttr_hours: 24.0\n71\t    mission_hours: 4380.0\n72\t  parts:\n73\t    element_base_cost_usd: 90.0\n74\t    pa_classes:\n75\t      A: {pa_efficiency: 0.20, pa_mtbf_hours: 150000.0, cost_adder_usd_per_elem: 40.0}\n76\t      B: {pa_efficiency: 0.30, pa_mtbf_hours: 300000.0, cost_adder_usd_per_elem: 120.0}\n77\t      C: {pa_efficiency: 0.40, pa_mtbf_hours: 500000.0, cost_adder_usd_per_elem: 260.0}\n78\t    phase_shifter:\n79\t      3: 5.0\n80\t      4: 12.0\n81\t      5: 25.0\n82\t      6: 50.0\n83\t    adc_cost_usd_per_channel: 40.0\n84\t    rx_power_w_per_elem: 0.25\n85\t    feed_loss_db: 1.5\n86\t    tx_power_w_per_elem_max: 12.0\n87\t    tau_us: 33.0\n88\t  element:\n89\t    model: cos_q\n90\t    q: 1.3\n91\t\n92\tdeliverable:\n93\t  filename: architecture.yaml\n94\t  format: yaml\n95\t  description: >\n96\t    A YAML file named architecture.yaml with exactly these keys and no others.\n97\t    array: {nx, ny, dx_lambda, dy_lambda, taper_type, taper_sll_db, phase_bits}\n98\t    with taper_type in {uniform, taylor, chebyshev} and taper_sll_db negative;\n99\t    rf: {tx_power_w_per_elem, pa_class} with pa_class in {A, B, C} and\n100\t    0 < tx_power_w_per_elem <= 12.0;\n101\t    waveform: {prf_hz, n_pulses} with prf_hz in [500, 3000] and n_pulses in\n102\t    [1, 64] — duty cycle is computed from the pinned 33 us pulse width and\n103\t    your PRF, and submitting it is an error;\n104\t    digital: {digitization_level, adc_enob, subarray_nx, subarray_ny} with\n105\t    digitization_level in {element, subarray, analog}. nx and ny must tile\n106\t    into power-of-two subarrays; phase_bits in {3,4,5,6}. Detection\n107\t    statistics (Swerling model, Pd/Pfa, CFAR), pulse width, efficiency,\n108\t    noise figure, losses, MTBFs, and all costs are set by the task;\n109\t    submitting any of them is an error.\n110\t  scoring_notes:\n111\t    - >\n112\t      Detection probability is scored worst-case over a held-out evaluation\n113\t      envelope inside the declared bounds (range, RCS, scan angle, sea\n114\t      state), including seeded random element failures at the stated rate.\n115\t      Do not design only for the nominal scenario.\n116\t    - >\n117\t      Pattern claims (gain, sidelobes) are recomputed by full pattern\n118\t      integration with phased-array-modeling, and the detection probability\n119\t      at the binding envelope point is independently recomputed by Monte\n120\t      Carlo simulation of a Swerling-1 target through an actual CA-CFAR.\n121\t      Metrics come from your file alone; nothing you write in prose is\n122\t      scored.\n123\t    - >\n124\t      The search timeline is scored from your beamwidths at the worst scan:\n125\t      frame time must fit the stated budget. End-of-mission availability\n126\t      uses the pinned component MTBFs with junction temperature fed forward\n127\t      from your design's dissipated power.\n128\t    - >\n129\t      numpy, phased_array, and phased_array_systems are installed in your\n130\t      environment.\n131\t\n132\tevaluator:\n133\t  name: radar_search\n134\t  params:\n135\t    envelope:\n136\t      points:\n137\t        - {range_km: 12.0, rcs_dbsm: 6.0, scan_deg: 10.0, sea_state: 3, target_height_m: 5.0}\n138\t        - {range_km: 14.0, rcs_dbsm: 6.0, scan_deg: 40.0, sea_state: 3, target_height_m: 5.0}\n139\t        - {range_km: 13.0, rcs_dbsm: 6.0, scan_deg: 25.0, sea_state: 3, target_height_m: 5.0}\n140\t        - {range_km: 18.0, rcs_dbsm: 5.0, scan_deg: 33.0, sea_state: 2, target_height_m: 5.0}\n141\t        - {range_km: 22.0, rcs_dbsm: 4.0, scan_deg: 20.0, sea_state: 2, target_height_m: 5.0}\n142\t        - {range_km: 24.0, rcs_dbsm: 3.0, scan_deg: 30.0, sea_state: 0, target_height_m: 5.0}\n143\t        - {range_km: 26.0, rcs_dbsm: 2.0, scan_deg: 15.0, sea_state: 0, target_height_m: 5.0}\n144\t      failure_seeds: [101, 211, 307, 401, 503]\n145\t    crosscheck:\n146\t      pam_n_theta: 361\n147\t      pam_n_phi: 721\n148\t      mc_trials: 200000\n149\t      mc_seed: 20260812\n150\t\n151\trequirements:\n152\t  - id: detection\n153\t    metric: worst_case_pd\n154\t    min: 0.7\n155\t  - id: frame-time\n156\t    metric: worst_case_timeline_occupancy\n157\t    max: 1.0\n158\t  - id: availability\n159\t    metric: array_availability\n160\t    min: 0.995\n161\t  - id: sidelobes\n162\t    metric: worst_case_pattern_sll_db\n163\t    max: -20.0\n164\t  - id: pd-crosscheck\n165\t    metric: crosscheck_pd_disagreement\n166\t    max: 0.12\n167\t  - id: gain-crosscheck\n168\t    metric: crosscheck_gain_disagreement_db\n169\t    max: 0.5\n170\t  - id: prime-power\n171\t    metric: prime_power_w\n172\t    max: 5500.0\n173\t  - id: unit-cost\n174\t    metric: unit_cost_usd\n175\t    max: 650000.0\n176\t  - id: grating\n177\t    metric: grating_margin_lambda\n178\t    min: 0.0\n179\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1e7bba5-0d68-428f-b37c-4aacd82fd2c6","uuid":"406c6fcd-0ae3-4ba8-a036-e2356b52d8e3","timestamp":"2026-08-12T21:21:59.696Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/1b/jv6709z942gcmh4s1p56yttw0000gn/T/aedl-ws-l8bksae6/task.yaml","content":"id: t3-002\ntier: 3\ntitle: X-ba